{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1000", "sample_idx": 11, "model_name": "meta/llama-3.2-3b-instruct", "content": "Raymond III Count of Tripoli was a member of the Banu Hamida dynasty and ruled over the County of Tripoli from 1149 to 1152. He was the son of Pons Count of Tripoli and was born around 1115. \n\n* **Early Life and Accession to the Throne ** \nRaymond III was born and raised in the County of Tripoli which was then a powerful and wealthy state. He was educated in the Byzantine Empire and later became a skilled military commander. In 1149 he succeeded his father as the Count of Tripoli and immediately began to consolidate his power and establish a strong military presence in the region.\n\n* **Military Campaigns and Alliances ** \nDuring his reign Raymond III led several military campaigns against the Zengid dynasty which controlled the neighboring County of Aleppo. He also formed alliances with other powerful noble families in the region including the Prince of Antioch. In 1149 he led a successful campaign against the Zengids and expanded the County of Tripoli's borders.\n\n* **Death and Legacy ** \nRaymond III died in 1152 from wounds sustained in a battle against the Mamluks. He was succeeded by his son Raymond IV who went on to rule the County of Tripoli for nearly 40 years. Raymond III's military campaigns and alliances had a lasting impact on the region and helped to establish the County of Tripoli as a major power in the Middle East. Despite his relatively short reign he left a lasting legacy and is remembered as a skilled and ambitious military leader.", "logprobs": [{"token": "Ray", "logprob": -0.001581966644152999}, {"token": "mond", "logprob": -3.576278118089249e-07}, {"token": " III", "logprob": -0.0001299296854995191}, {"token": " Count", "logprob": -0.1985016018152237}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -3.194758028257638e-05}, {"token": " Trip", "logprob": -0.0002616301644593477}, {"token": "oli", "logprob": -6.01988795096986e-05}, {"token": " w